# Cyborg interludes — short broadcast-only beats the Playwright can
# splice in between any other beat to crank the tension. Not on the
# main divert tree; the Playwright invokes them with booth_force_
# directive lines or by manual divert from the simulator.

== plaza_glitch
  cast: Player
  setting: Plaza

<broadcast: location(Plaza)>
  NARRATOR
    Every screen in the Plaza shows the same frame for one second
    longer than it should. Then they resume.

CYBORG
  (improv duration: 20s, advance on: any [gesture(notice)])
  (Walk through the Plaza in step with another cyborg. Make no eye
   contact. Stop exactly mid-crossing. Resume.)

-> END

== chatter_glitch
  cast: Player
  setting: ChatterCamp

<broadcast: cohort(Chatters) and location(ChatterCamp)>
  NARRATOR
    A sticker on the back wall, which definitely was a peace sign a
    minute ago, is now a crown.

CYBORG
  (improv duration: 20s, advance on: any [speech(go), gesture(Cue)])
  (From the doorway, in chorus with one off-stage voice: "VEX.")

<set: Vex.trusts.Chatters -= 5>

-> END

== mod_glitch
  cast: Player
  setting: ModOutpost

<broadcast: cohort(Mods) and location(ModOutpost)>
  NARRATOR
    Every monitor on the back wall, for one frame, shows the chair
    in the Core. No one knows what it is yet.

<set: Praxis.knows.motherboard_named = true>

-> END
